  -- TheoryBase and LiteratureBase links
   $J$TheoryBase proposition: the problem in evolution teaching is not purposive language as such but whether a trait is explained by design (an agent or a need) or by selection (differential survival and reproduction). Strand 2, stage GB-3 puts Montessori's Cosmic Task idea next to this claim and asks how the Cosmic Task wording actually lands in children's reasoning. Nobody has studied that.$J$,
   NULL, $J$TheoryBase carries this record as an author draft (review_status author-draft). No maturity level is claimed here.$J$, 'theorybase', 'OE-PROPOSITION-selection-teleology-legitimate'),
  ('dbf78689-3bf8-5e94-afb1-d28beb1c0aab', v_en, $J$Learning Progressions as Scientific Models$J$,
   $J$A learning progression is treated as a scientific model that can be checked against evidence. The Cosmic Education LPM writes a century-old pedagogy down precisely enough (age bands, concepts, observable indicators) to be checked this way. It has not been checked yet.$J$,
   'theoretically-developed', NULL, 'theorybase', 'OE-THEORY-learning-progressions-as-scientific-models')
  ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

  ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

